389: ## 5. SETTLED PREMISES -- re-inlined so nobody spends an answer re-deriving them
390: 
391: Settled by this round's drafting, each RE-READ at HEAD `0b09e7b6` in THIS scope (line numbers as read; the same in the
392: working tree) or by the witness run (section 2):
393: 
394: * **S1** `le_register_write()` 839-888: `case 0:` handles CSR0 bit by bit (844-882); `default:` stores whole, 884-886.
395:   Its only caller is `DEVICE_ACCESS(le)` line 1002, passing `d->reg_select`; the RAP write arm stores
396:   `d->reg_select = idata & (N_REGISTERS - 1)` (1015) with `N_REGISTERS` 4 (79) -- so `r` is always in {0,1,2,3} and
397:   `default:` serves exactly CSR1, CSR2, CSR3.  (Measured: `rap mask` 0x13 -> 0x0003.)
398: * **S2** `uint16_t reg[N_REGISTERS]` (99); `x` is `uint32_t` (839); the store already truncates to 16 bits.
399: * **S3** The RDP read returns `d->reg[d->reg_select]` unmasked (981); the common tail `do_return:` writes `odata` and
400:   ticks the device (1036-1045).  For CSR1-3 the read-back is the guest's only direct channel.
401: * **S4** The register window is registered `DM_DEFAULT` at `baseaddr + 0x100000` (1108-1109); on the KN01 `baseaddr` is
402:   `KN01_SYS_LANCE` = 0x18000000 (`dec_kn01.h` 136; `machine_pmax.c` 129-131) -> registers at physical 0x18100000,
403:   RDP = KSEG1 0xb8100000, RAP = 0xb8100004, 16-bit ports.  `DM_DEFAULT` means the debugger's `dump`/`put` do not
404:   reach the handler, which is why the probe drives it with guest `sh`/`lhu`.  Witnessed by the two signature rows.
405: * **S5** Reset state: `d->reg[0] = LE_STOP` (1077) = 0x0004 (`if_lereg.h` 363); `reg[1..3]` are 0 from the `memset`
406:   (1060).  Measured: `csr0 reset` 0x0004.
407: * **S6** Readers of `reg[1..3]`: `le_chip_init` 179 builds `init_block_addr` from `reg[1] & 0xffff` and
408:   `reg[2] & 0xff`; 180-182 warns on an odd address; **`reg[3]` is read nowhere** (`grep -n 'reg\[3\]'` matches
409:   nothing; BSWP/ACON/BCON configure bus byte lanes the model does not emulate).  So CSR3's only observable is its
410:   read-back, CSR2's reserved byte is already invisible to the consumer, and CSR1's bit 0 reaches only the parity warning.
411: * **S7** `le_register_write` is non-static and has exactly one caller in the tree (1002).
412: * **S8** `if_lereg.h` defines `LE_CSR0..3` (344-347), `LE_BSWP 0x4` (367), `LE_MODE 0x0` (368); no ACON/BCON names
413:   exist in the tree.
414: * **S9** The datasheet lines quoted in 9.1 are READINGS of `am79c90_bitsavers.txt`, cross-checked identical in
415:   `am79c90_mit.txt`; whether the C-LANCE text binds the Am7990 model is P2.
416: * **S10** `dev_le.c` is identical at HEAD, in the working tree and in `est/` (section 4); its last change was
417:   `5bf592d6` (2026-07-26).
418: * **S11** The witness: binary `6c27af7b` built from a git-archive export of HEAD `0b09e7b6`; 17/17 HEAD column,
419:   CONTROL=OK; the detector revision 18/18 HEAD column on the same binary (2.1-2.3).
420: * **S12** The probe never writes CSR0's STRT or INIT, so every CSR1-3 write it makes happens with STOP set -- the state
