474: ## 7. The partition, cells, rows and variants -- as DATA: check them, do not ratify them
475: 
476: **7.1 Partition of inputs.**  (register `r`, bit `b`, STOP state, access width).  The repair changes what the model
477: STORES (and therefore reads back) for exactly: `r = 1, b = 0`; `r = 2, b in 8..15`; `r = 3, b in 3..15`.  It leaves
478: alone: `r = 0` (any bit; a different arm); `r = 1, b in 1..15`; `r = 2, b in 0..7`; `r = 3, b in 0..2`.  STOP state and
479: width do not enter the edited arm's own tests (S12, P8).
480: 
481: **7.2 The floor** (R1-R4):
482: * **(a)** the probe in GATE mode (FIX column) on the pre-fix build: predicted **14/18**, the four symptom rows red
483:   (leg L0, 7.7).
484: * **(b)** verbatim reinstatement of `d->reg[r] = x;` at the one fixed site = the pre-fix build: 14/18 (V1).
485: * **(c)** null medium, a runtime probe: an absent / non-emulator binary -- `(c): measured at <killtable artifact>`,
486:   planned as leg L3 with `/bin/false`; predicted 0/18, CONTROL=FAIL (P12).
487: * **(d)** DEPENDS-ON: the predicate dominating the edited lines inside `le_register_write` is `switch (r)` with the
488:   labels {1, 2, 3}; the body masks `x` and tests nothing on it, so each label's generating set is {its kept bits, its
489:   dropped bits}, with the boundary bits -- CSR1 bits 0/1, CSR2 bits 7/8, CSR3 bits 2/3 -- the D2 edges (R5).
490:   **Cells C1-C6:** C1 CSR1 dropped (bit 0) A� C2 CSR1 kept (bits 1 and 15 rowed) A� C3 CSR2 dropped (15:8) A�
491:   C4 CSR2 kept (7:0) A� C5 CSR3 dropped (15:3) A� C6 CSR3 kept (2:0).  All six are rowed (7.4).
492:   **Not cells (clause (e), R6):** the STOP state (S12, P7); the access width (P8); the CSR0 arm; big-endian hosts
493:   (3.3); the INIT path (no INIT is issued).
494: 
495: **7.3 Sibling parity.**  One arm serves three labels, so the siblings are the LABELS.  Each has an ALL row (write 0xffff;
496: reads back exactly the mask, so ANY single change M -> M' to that register's mask reds it: 0xffff & M' = M' != M) and
497: a KEPT row with the kept boundary bit set (CSR1 0x1236 bit 1; CSR2 0x00a5 bit 7; CSR3 0x0005 bit 2).  CSR1 additionally
498: carries `odd` (the research row's named symptom; the dropped boundary bit alone) and `top` (bit 15).  The asymmetry --
499: no `0x0100`-only row for CSR2, no `0x0008`-only row for CSR3 -- is covered by the ALL rows under the claim just stated;
500: **check that claim rather than the count.**
501: 
502: **7.4 Rows N1-N18** (the shipping revision; one fresh emulator per session; wants are literals; `channel` names the
503: observable that differs and the variant it reds on):
504: 
505: | # | row | session | stimulus | HEAD | FIX | kind | channel (reds on) |
506: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
507: | N1-N4 | `ram:<s>` | each | `sh`/`lhu` 0x5a5a via KSEG0 RAM | 0x5a5a | 0x5a5a | control | liveness; a dead run (V20) |
508: | N5 | `csr0 reset` | csr0 | RAP=0, read RDP | 0x0004 | 0x0004 | control | device signature; V20; a window translation (R7) |
509: | N6 | `rap mask` | csr0 | RAP:=0x13, read RAP | 0x0003 | 0x0003 | control | signature; V20 |
510: | N7 | `csr3 all` | csr3 | RAP=3, write 0xffff, read | 0xffff | **0x0007** | symptom | read-back; V1 V7 V8 V9 V11 V18 V19 |

