The review found three corrections to the accepted reasoning: “write as zeroes” does not prove zero storage after an invalid write; the quoted floor rules do not make an AND mask a comparison boundary test; and shifting the register window by four bytes does not swap both ports. The CSR3-only repair and the proposed 19 rows remain defensible.

